<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <%- include('head') %>
  <title><%= locals.title %></title>
  <meta name="description" content="<%= locals.description %>" />
  <meta property="og:title" content="<%= locals.title %>" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="<%= locals.description %>" />
  <%- include('og-image') %>
  <meta property="og:url" content="<%= siteUrl %>/privacy-policy" />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="<%= siteName %>" />
</head>

<body class="layout">
  <%- include('navbar') %> <%- include('left-sidebar') %>
  <main>
    <div class="container">
      <%- include('flash') %>
      <%# Drawn here because the page is indexable now, and views/head.ejs
          writes a BreadcrumbList for it from the same `breadcrumbs` local:
          structured data is meant to describe what a reader can see, so the
          trail in the markup and the trail in the JSON-LD arrive together.
          Same pairing as views/about.ejs. %>
      <%- include('breadcrumb') %>
      <section>
        <h1 class="text-lg" style="margin-bottom: 5px">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p style="
              color: rgb(var(--muted-rgb));
              font-size: 0.9em;
              margin-bottom: 25px;
            ">
          Last updated: March 2026
        </p>

        <p style="margin-bottom: 20px">
          This Privacy Policy describes how
          <strong>OldSchoolGames.eu</strong> ("we", "us", "our") collects,
          uses, and protects your personal data when you use this website. We
          are committed to protecting your privacy, and this policy is written
          to describe the site accurately rather than to claim more than it
          does. It follows the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and
          applicable EU/Czech data protection law, with one departure we would
          rather name than bury: the analytics cookies in section 2(b) are set
          on your first visit, before you are asked. That section says what
          they are and how to refuse them.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">
          1. Data Controller
        </h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          The data controller responsible for this website is:<br />
          <strong>RobLib</strong><br />
          Czech Republic<br />
          Email:
          <a class="color-primary underline" href="mailto:contact@oldschoolgames.eu">contact@oldschoolgames.eu</a>
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">
          2. What Data We Collect
        </h2>

        <h3 style="margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 600">a) Comments</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          Anyone can post a comment without creating an account. When you post
          a comment, we store the comment text, an optional display name
          (nickname) you provide, and a timestamp. If no nickname is given, the
          comment is posted as <em>anonymous</em>. Comments are publicly
          visible.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 600">
          b) Usage data (Google Analytics)
        </h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to understand how
          visitors use the site. This service collects anonymized information
          including pages visited, time spent on pages, device type, and
          approximate geographic location (country/region level). IP addresses
          are anonymized. Google Analytics sets cookies in your browser. For
          more information, see
          <a class="color-primary underline" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          These cookies are set on every visit, and they are set without
          asking you first — this site shows no consent banner. If you would
          rather they were not set, you can block them in your browser's settings, refuse
          third-party or all cookies for this site, or use one of the browser
          extensions that block analytics scripts — the site works exactly the
          same either way, and nothing here checks whether analytics loaded.
          Clearing this site's cookies removes them again.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 600">
          c) Browser-local storage (favorites & recently played)
        </h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          Your favorite games and recently played games are stored in your
          browser's <strong>localStorage</strong> as a list of game
          identifiers. The list never leaves your device except to ask our
          server for the current title and artwork of those games, and we do
          not store or link that request to you.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 600">d) Game ratings</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          Ratings are attributed to a first-party cookie
          (<strong>osg_vid</strong>) containing a randomly generated
          identifier that expires after one year. It is set on your first page
          view rather than when you actually vote — it has to already be there
          for the stars to show you a rating you gave earlier — and it exists
          solely so that one browser counts as one vote. It contains no
          personal data and is not used for advertising or for tracking across
          other sites. When you do rate a game we also store the IP address of
          that vote for abuse prevention, and delete it again after 90 days.
          Deleting the cookie simply lets you rate again.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 600">
          e) Cookies the site itself needs
        </h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          Two more first-party cookies are set for the site to work at all.
          Neither is used for analytics, advertising or tracking across other
          sites, and neither carries anything about you.
        </p>
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; line-height: 2; margin-bottom: 15px">
          <li>
            <strong>osg_csrf</strong> — a random value set on your first page
            view and kept for one month. Every form on this site has to echo
            it back, which is what stops another website submitting a comment,
            a rating or an administrator's form on your behalf. It identifies
            nobody: it is the same kind of random number as a coin toss, and
            it is read only to compare it against what a form sent.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>connect.sid</strong> — set only when an administrator logs
            in, and cleared when they log out. It holds nothing but a
            reference to a server-side session, expires after 30 days, and is
            never set for ordinary visitors.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          Both are strictly necessary for the site to function and are listed
          here for completeness rather than because they are optional —
          blocking them means forms and logging in stop working.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 600">
          f) Abuse prevention and server logs
        </h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          Every request to this site is counted against a limit, so that one
          visitor cannot flood the comment form, the rating stars or the login
          page. The counter is keyed by your <strong>IP address</strong>, which
          means the address is briefly stored in our database alongside a
          number of requests and an expiry time. Nothing else is recorded with
          it, it is never linked to your comments, ratings or analytics data,
          and it is <strong>deleted within 25 minutes</strong> — the longest
          counting window is 15 minutes and expired entries are swept away
          every 10.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          The server also writes one line per request to its log — the method
          and the address requested, which for a search includes the words you
          searched for. These lines carry <strong>no IP address</strong> and
          nothing else identifying you. They go to our hosting provider's log
          collector, which discards them on its own schedule; we keep no copy
          of our own.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">
          3. Legal Basis for Processing
        </h2>
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; line-height: 2; margin-bottom: 15px">
          <li>
            <strong>Comments:</strong> Legitimate interest (enabling community
            interaction; no account or personal data required)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Strictly necessary cookies</strong> (osg_csrf, osg_vid,
            connect.sid): Necessary for the service you asked for — form
            protection, one vote per browser, and keeping an administrator
            logged in. They store no personal data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Abuse prevention</strong> (the IP address behind a
            rate-limit counter, and the IP address recorded with a rating):
            Legitimate interest in keeping the site usable — protecting the
            comment form, the rating stars and the login page from flooding.
            Both are kept for no longer than that needs: minutes for the
            counter, 90 days for a vote.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Legitimate interest in knowing
            how many people visit the site and which games they look at, so it
            can be maintained and improved. The reports behind it are
            aggregate visitor counts; no attempt is made to identify anyone or
            to follow a visitor across other sites.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">4. Data Sharing</h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          We do not sell or rent your personal data. We share anonymized usage
          data with Google via Google Analytics. Our hosting provider stores
          the site's database and collects its server logs on our behalf, as a
          processor acting under our instructions. No other third parties
          receive your personal data.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">5. Data Retention</h2>
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; line-height: 2; margin-bottom: 15px">
          <li>
            <strong>Comments:</strong> Retained until an administrator removes
            them. Because comments are posted without an account, we have no
            way to link them to you after submission — if you need a comment
            removed, please contact us.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Game ratings:</strong> The rating itself is kept for as
            long as the game is listed. The IP address recorded alongside it
            is deleted after 90 days — the rating, which carries no personal
            data, stays.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Play counts:</strong> A record that a game was started
            (the game and the time, nothing identifying you) is kept for 12
            months and then deleted.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Rate-limit counters:</strong> The IP address behind a
            counter is deleted within 25 minutes of your last request — see
            2f) above.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Server logs:</strong> Kept by our hosting provider on
            their own schedule; they contain no IP address and we keep no copy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cookies:</strong> osg_vid expires after one year, osg_csrf
            after one month, and an administrator's connect.sid after 30 days
            or when they log out, whichever comes first. Clearing this site's
            cookies removes all three immediately.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Retained for 14 months per
            Google's default settings.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">
          6. Your Rights (GDPR)
        </h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 10px">
          Under GDPR, you have the following rights:
        </p>
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; line-height: 2; margin-bottom: 15px">
          <li>
            <strong>Right of access</strong> — request a copy of your personal
            data
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to rectification</strong> — request correction of
            inaccurate data
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to erasure</strong> — request deletion of your
            personal data ("right to be forgotten")
          </li>
          <li><strong>Right to restrict processing</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong></li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to object</strong> to processing based on legitimate
            interest
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
          <a class="color-primary underline" href="mailto:contact@oldschoolgames.eu">contact@oldschoolgames.eu</a>. We will respond within 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">7. Security</h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          All data is transmitted over HTTPS. We take reasonable technical and
          organisational measures to protect your data against unauthorised
          access.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">
          8. Changes to This Policy
        </h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px">
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "last
          updated" date at the top of this page will reflect any changes.
          Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of
          the revised policy.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-md" style="margin: 25px 0 10px">9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any privacy-related questions or requests, email us at
          <a class="color-primary underline" href="mailto:contact@oldschoolgames.eu">contact@oldschoolgames.eu</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <%- include('right-sidebar') %> <%- include('footer') %>
</body>

</html>
